<div style="background-color: #dbe9f4; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.2em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Panama's Role in the World</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> How the Canal Impacts Panama's Future</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write analytical reports on current topics like social trends or global events. Interactive: Produce a collaborative story on local or global interest topics.</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write analytical reports on the Panama Canal's effects, comparing revenue statistics and environmental findings (e.g., "Since the expansion, the Canal has increased annual profits by three billion dollars but has also reduced water levels in surrounding lakes.")<br>Can collaborate on writing a story about Panama's global impact, discussing its role in trade (e.g., "Panama has always played an important role in global trade, thanks to the Panama Canal. If Panama invested more in its infrastructure, it could become an even more powerful trade hub in the future.")<br>Can work with classmates to outline a report on Panama's trade role, discussing key aspects like economic growth (e.g., "Let's include sections on shipping routes and local job creation.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b><br>Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a thought-provoking image of the Panama Canal's expansion or a modern container ship navigating it. Students are given 2 minutes to individually write down 3-5 sentences describing how they think the Canal 'influences' global trade or Panama's 'future', using any related vocabulary they recall.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes an example sentence on the board using passive voice and target vocabulary: "Global relationships *have been enhanced* by the Canal's efficient operation since its construction." The teacher then writes a conditional sentence: "If Panama *had not invested* in the expansion, global traffic *would have faced* significant delays." The teacher models the pronunciation of 'global' /oʊ/ and 'environmental' /ɪnˌvaɪ.rənˈmen.təl/ as they read the sentences.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"In 'Global relationships have been enhanced...', is the focus on 'relationships' or 'the Canal'?" (Relationships)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Does 'If Panama had not invested...' talk about a real past event or a hypothetical past event?" (A hypothetical past event)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b><br>Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Panama's Role in the World".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short excerpt (approx. 120 words) from an academic report titled "The Panama Canal: A Nexus of Global Trade and Environmental Stewardship," provided as a handout or projected. The text describes the Canal's economic and environmental 'impacts', integrating passive voice, second/third conditionals, and present perfect continuous, using target vocabulary such as 'efficiency', 'investments', 'environmental groups', 'ecosystems', 'authority', and 'global relationships'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Understand and interpret written information about global events and local issues, specifically analytical reports on the Panama Canal's impact.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the report excerpt individually.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What are the two main types of impact the report discusses regarding the Panama Canal?" (Economic and environmental impacts).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Students match phrases from the text to complete sentences about the Canal's 'operation' and 'future' (e.g., "The Canal's 'authority' has been...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students then underline all sentences that contain the passive voice, second/third conditionals, or the present perfect continuous.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b><br>Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Writing sentences and paragraphs using passive voice, second and third conditionals, present perfect continuous, and specified vocabulary (e.g., 'operations', 'investments', 'environmental concerns', 'trade', 'impact').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled practice: Sentence Transformation (5 min):</b> Students work individually on a handout. They rewrite active sentences into passive voice (e.g., "The government operates the Canal." -> "The Canal *is operated* by the government."), complete conditional sentences (e.g., "If there ____ (not be) a Canal, global shipping ____ (face) greater costs."), and fill in blanks with the present perfect continuous (e.g., "Environmental groups ____ (monitor) the ecosystems for years."). They must use target vocabulary from the provided list.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled practice: Paragraph Completion (5 min):</b> In pairs, students receive a short paragraph outline about a hypothetical future scenario for the Canal. They must complete the paragraph with their own ideas, ensuring they use at least one example of passive voice, one second/third conditional, and one present perfect continuous sentence. The paragraph should integrate at least three specific vocabulary words (e.g., 'infrastructure', 'efficiency', 'sustainable').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Peer Check & Feedback (3 min):</b> Pairs exchange their completed paragraphs with another pair. They check each other's work for correct grammar and appropriate vocabulary use, specifically looking for the target grammatical structures. They provide constructive written feedback on clarity and accuracy.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">13 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b><br>Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Panama's Role in the World".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format: Collaborative Analytical Paragraph Writing.</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">In groups of three, students collaboratively write an analytical paragraph (6-8 sentences) for a report on the topic: "How future 'investments' in the Panama Canal's 'infrastructure' could impact 'global relationships' and 'environmental concerns'."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The paragraph must:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Include at least two sentences in the passive voice (e.g., "New technologies *could be implemented*...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Contain at least one second or third conditional sentence expressing a hypothetical future impact (e.g., "If more funds *were allocated* to green technologies, the Canal *would become* more 'sustainable'.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Feature at least one sentence in the present perfect continuous discussing ongoing developments (e.g., "The 'authority' *has been considering* new strategies...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Incorporate at least five target vocabulary words relevant to the theme (e.g., 'investments', 'infrastructure', 'global relationships', 'environmental groups', 'efficiency', 'future').</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students are encouraged to express hypothetical ideas and discuss the Canal's 'impact' respectfully, using specific trade-related terms appropriately. The teacher circulates, offering support and monitoring the use of target structures and vocabulary.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b><br>Formative assessment strategy and student self-reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation during the collaborative writing and review of submitted paragraphs using a checklist for grammatical accuracy and vocabulary use. Peer assessment (from Stage 3) also contributes.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Groups submit their collaboratively written analytical paragraph from Stage 4.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of passive voice (2-3 examples).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct formation and use of second/third conditionals (at least 1 example).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of present perfect continuous (at least 1 example).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Integration of at least five target vocabulary words.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity, coherence, and respectful tone in discussing Panama's 'impact' on trade.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Overall grammatical accuracy and sentence structure.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two short prompts before leaving:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did I effectively use the passive voice and conditionals to express hypothetical ideas about the Canal's future impact?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most challenging part of collaborating on writing this analytical paragraph?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b><br>Student and teacher reflection for continuous improvement.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection Prompts:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new insights did I gain about the Panama Canal's 'influence' on 'global trade' today and in the 'future' through this writing task?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How confident do I feel now about writing analytical sentences using passive voice, conditionals, and present perfect continuous?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this writing lesson? (e.g., student engagement with the collaborative task, specific grammar points were applied accurately).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What challenges arose? (e.g., consistent use of third conditionals, vocabulary spelling, maintaining respectful tone).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson to improve writing skills and content integration? (e.g., more structured sentence frames for conditionals, a peer editing checklist focusing on specific vocabulary).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), students will mediate information from their reports and other sources to create a consolidated presentation or summary on the Canal's 'global impact', further developing their ability to express and synthesize complex ideas in English, potentially leading to a larger 21st Century Skills Project.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>